{"name":"Doctor","hex":"#f9f9f9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Doctor","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Short for Fremantle Doctor."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The title of an academic or medical doctor; used before or instead of the doctor's name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Doctor"}],"entries":[{"title":"Medical doctor","blocks":[{"text":"A medical doctor, also known as a physician or medical practitioner, is a health professional who practices medicine. Medicine aims to promote, maintain or restore health through the study, diagnosis, prognosis and treatment of disease, injury, and other physical and mental conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/The_Doctor_Luke_Fildes_crop.jpg/330px-The_Doctor_Luke_Fildes_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medical_doctor"},{"title":"Doctor (title)","blocks":[{"text":"Doctor is an academic title that originates from the Latin word of the same spelling. The word is originally an agentive noun of the Latin verb docēre 'to teach' and thus translates directly to teacher. It has been used as an academic title in Europe since the 13th century, when the first doctorates were awarded at the University of Bologna and the University of Paris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Aquatint_of_a_Doctor_in_divinity_at_the_University_of_Oxford%2C_shown_wearing_convocation_dress.jpg/330px-Aquatint_of_a_Doctor_in_divinity_at_the_University_of_Oxford%2C_shown_wearing_convocation_dress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_(title)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Francesco_Redi.jpg/500px-Francesco_Redi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.